        "review_id": 125269811,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r125269811-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "A Sacred Highlight & a Must See Experience",
        "text": "We stayed at Dwarika Hotel and were able to walk to the Pashupatinath temple complex \nin about 20 minutes and we mingled with the street venders who sold weird and wonderful food as well as tacky souvenirs.\nIt is a sacred sight  which was very rambling and there is so much to see.We were not allowed to enter the temple but this did not detract from our visit in any way. The main sites for us were over the bridge and on the riverbank. There are several cremation Ghats and a number of them were in use. I must confess to a morbid fascination of watching several embalmed bodies in various states of cremation. Why? I ask myself, I suppose it is so different from my culture that I found it so captivating. I was also captivated(again) with the variety of holy men who paint themselves from head to toe in strange bright colours. Not sure if this is a gimmick as they are more than happy to pose for a photograph providing you give them a tip!\nPlenty of other temple sights to see, be warned of the monkeys, they are everywhere and so many of them and it is advisable to not eat food as you are liable to lose it! The other warning is that the place is very dirty with rubbish strewn everywhere. However, do not let this put you off, this is a sacred hindu temple and an experience you are unlikely to repeat.",
