        "title": "like an exciting TV documentary",
        "text": "our tour guide decided to bring us to Pashupatinath in the morning because they were having cremation ceremonies in the morning beside the river. We never entered the temple but viewed from across the river, which gave us a great vantage point to observe the cremation rituals. What as sight! while we were there, we saw one that just finished, another one ongoing, and a third starting. One of them was a rich and famous Nepali so you could see the dramatic contrast in preparation, rituals, number of well-wishers, number of dhalit workers, etc. You read about it but it doesn't get to you until you actually see it happen in front of your eyes. Of course, the tour guide has to be beside you giving you the background and insights. ",
