        "title": "Overwhelming",
        "text": "A very interesting place to visit and learn a slice of hindu belief. But when there is an ongoing open cremation, the smell can be quite overpowering (like burning hair magnified). I was watching one taking place while standing on the bridge in the temple grounds. There were 4 sadhus (hindu holy men) in colorful face painting and apparel. My friend told me that they are from India, not Nepal. They can be photographed with anyone for a price. For a more reflective moment, the events in this place make one think about earthly life in the perspective of eternity, like the mist in the morning and gone in a short while.",
