      {
        "review_id": 123893868,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r123893868-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "all  devotees  can  see  the  lord  clearly  from  a  distance",
        "text": "Here  lord  Shiva can  be  seen  in   ancient  form (animal  face)  facing  four  directions . Nice  arrangement ,so  that  all  devotees  can  see  the  lord  clearly  from  a  distance  ,  so  that  ( wooden  sloping  stairs  with  a  landing  in  the  middle  facing  the  front  of  lord  Shiva)  but  one  has  to  move  in  a  queue to  see  all  four  faces  of  the  lord  and  complete  a  parikrama (a complete round) . Large  premises  with  a  lots  of other  deities  .A  large  Kal  Bhairav   idol  , the  priest  (woman)  gives   a  heavy  punch  on  the  back  of  every  devotee  while  leaning  against  the  idol ,  it  is  said  to  eradicate  all  evils  of  life . On  the  other  side  of  the  temple  the  sacred  Bagmati  river (now  heavily  polluted ) where  the  human  corps  being  cremated  and  the  ashes  were  thrown in  to  the  river. There  were  lots  of  human  bodies  in  the  river  bank  waited  for  the  rituals ,  which  reminded  the  scene  of  our  Swarga  Dwara  ( Puri  dham –Orissa-India) . The  evening   Arati  is  special  ,  one  must  attend . The  shops  on  the way  to  Pashupatinath  sell  different  types of  salagrams  ( one  must    have  the  ability  to  identify  them ).  By  the  way  we  can  buy  the original  Rudrakhya  and  salagram  from  Nepal  .",
